> is x even and x odd?
  note: "even": read as an even function, f(-x) = f(x), not an even number for every input (say "an even function" or "always even")
  ucas: it(x) = x where x % 2 != 0
  ucas: parity it
  note: x has no type: inferred int from the integer operations in the body
parity of it:
  odd: f(-x) = -f(x)
  not even: f(x) = 1, f(-x) = -1 at x = 1
  proved, exhaustive over every x with -x in the domain
> is x even and x odd and x even?
  note: "even": read as an even function, f(-x) = f(x), not an even number for every input (say "an even function" or "always even")
  ucas: it(x) = x where x % 2 == 0, x % 2 != 0
  ucas: parity it
  note: x has no type: inferred int from the integer operations in the body
parity of it:
  neither (parity does not apply)
  proved, exhaustive over every x with -x in the domain
